8250: CE5300 GEN3 UART needs DMA_SELECT + a 64-byte FIFO in the port config

The last piece of the IO-MCU bring-up. Everything else is in place — the ports
run polled (0002), forced to PORT_XSCALE with UUE (0006), TX driven from the LSR
(0010), and the shadowing PCI UART is gone (0011) — yet ttyS1 still transmitted
into silence: the FIFO loaded, LSR read empty, but nothing reached the tm4c
(proven with a known-good emitter->GC-IRL rig that captures 35/35 from stock and
0 from openHC).

The difference is the PORT_XSCALE port config itself. Mainline gives it a 32-byte
FIFO and fcr = ENABLE_FIFO | R_TRIG_10. Control4's kernel (intel_kernel_patches/
00178030) renames the same PORT_XSCALE to "GEN3_serial" and sets a 64-byte FIFO
AND UART_FCR_DMA_SELECT. On this SoC's UART block that FCR bit is not cosmetic —
it is what makes the transmitter actually drive its pin. The console (ttyS0)
escaped the problem only because CEFDK had already set its FCR up before Linux;
ttyS1 is configured by Linux from the mainline table, so it never got DMA_SELECT.

Bring the PORT_XSCALE config in line with stock's GEN3 values. Applies to every
port forced to XScale here, which is what stock does too.

Scope: EA family only (board/ea-common/patches). Pairs with 0002/0006/0010/0011.

Author: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_port.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/8250/8250_port.c
@@ -146,9 +146,19 @@
 	},
 	[PORT_XSCALE] = {
 		.name		= "XScale",
-		.fifo_size	= 32,
-		.tx_loadsz	= 32,
-		.fcr		= UART_FCR_ENABLE_FIFO | UART_FCR_R_TRIG_10,
+		/*
+		 * Intel CE5300 (EA family): Control4's kernel calls PORT_XSCALE
+		 * "GEN3_serial" and gives it a 64-byte FIFO and, crucially,
+		 * UART_FCR_DMA_SELECT. On this SoC's UART block that bit is what
+		 * makes the transmitter actually drive the pin; without it the FIFO
+		 * loads and LSR reads empty but nothing reaches the wire (the IO-MCU
+		 * on ttyS1 stays silent, rx=0). The console (ttyS0) escaped this
+		 * because CEFDK set its FCR up; ttyS1 is configured by Linux. Match
+		 * stock's GEN3 values. EA-only patch dir.
+		 */
+		.fifo_size	= 64,
+		.tx_loadsz	= 64,
+		.fcr		= UART_FCR_ENABLE_FIFO | UART_FCR_DMA_SELECT | UART_FCR_R_TRIG_10,
 		.flags		= UART_CAP_FIFO | UART_CAP_UUE | UART_CAP_RTOIE,
 	},
 	[PORT_OCTEON] = {
